From a45cf1f8a9715f32b0cf03a4e5fa92a07f9155b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:06:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 42/48] perf(audio): do not wake the XMA worker after an inline
 kick decode

A context kick decodes the kicked contexts at once on the writing
thread, and XmaContext::Work takes the context lock and clears the
enable before it decodes, so by the end of the kick none of them is left
for the worker. The kick still set work_event_, and the woken worker
walked all 320 contexts, about 18 KB apart, reading each one's enable
flag and finding nothing to do.

In Project Gotham Racing 4 on a Steam Deck that sweep was 8.6 % of a
core, 71 % of it on the enable load (one cache miss per context). With
the wake removed the worker stays idle, the game's audio thread went
from 52 % to 47 % of a core and a scripted race from 69.1 to 70.6 fps.

Pause, resume and shutdown still set the event, and a context whose
kick finds it locked by the worker waits on the lock and decodes after
it, so nothing is left pending.

Xenia Canary has no inline decode (XmaDecoder::WriteRegister only wakes
work_event_ on a kick, src/xenia/apu/xma_decoder.cc at 451f915); this
change only concerns ReXGlue's inline path.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/audio/xma_decoder.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/xma_decoder.cpp b/src/audio/xma_decoder.cpp
index a0a178d..4366dfc 100644
--- a/src/audio/xma_decoder.cpp
+++ b/src/audio/xma_decoder.cpp
@@ -304,7 +304,8 @@ void XmaDecoder::WriteRegister(uint32_t addr, uint32_t value) {
         }
       }
     }
-    work_event_->Set();
+    // Work() consumes the enable, so every kicked context is done by now. Waking
+    // the worker here only made it sweep all contexts and find nothing.
   } else if (r >= XmaRegister::Context0Lock && r <= XmaRegister::Context9Lock) {
     // Context lock command.
     // This requests a lock by flagging the context.
-- 
